  <!-- FAQ -->
  <section class="faq-section">
    <div class="why-header">
      <div class="eyebrow eyebrow--brand" style="font-size:12px">Spec Questions · 07</div>
      <div class="eyebrow" style="font-size:11px">Frequently asked · spec writer &amp; designer</div>
    </div>
    <h2 class="faq-h2">The questions a designer asks before specifying the lamp.</h2>
    <div class="faq-list">
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q"><div class="faq-num">01</div><div class="faq-text">Are these vintage-look LEDs or actual filament bulbs?</div></div>
        <div class="faq-a">LED. The amber glass and visible filament strands are real, but the light source is a chip-on-board or filament-style LED inside. You get the look of an Edison incandescent at 4–8W instead of 40–60W, with 15,000-hour rated life.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q"><div class="faq-num">02</div><div class="faq-text">Which lamps are dim-to-warm?</div></div>
        <div class="faq-a">The full Signature line dims 2700K → 2200K on a phase-cut wall dimmer. Vintage Decor G25 and CA10 are dim-to-warm at the PRO+ tier. tubul<span style="color:var(--color-alg-red)">Ⓐ</span>RCH and Nostalgic Decor hold a fixed CCT through the dim curve — pick by warmth, not by transition.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q"><div class="faq-num">03</div><div class="faq-text">Are these Title 20 / JA8 compliant for California spec?</div></div>
        <div class="faq-a">Signature is ENERGY STAR listed and meets Title 20 across all four shapes. Vintage Decor A19 and G25 are JA8-rated when ordered with the JA8 driver option. Nostalgic Decor and tubul<span style="color:var(--color-alg-red)">Ⓐ</span>RCH are decorative-rated; check the spec sheet for the specific application.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q"><div class="faq-num">04</div><div class="faq-text">What dimmer should I pair with these?</div></div>
        <div class="faq-a">Phase-cut leading-edge or trailing-edge wall dimmers from Lutron, Leviton, or Legrand. The compatibility list ships on the spec sheet. Avoid 0–10V — these are decorative E26 / E12 base lamps, not driver-controlled luminaires.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q"><div class="faq-num">05</div><div class="faq-text">Do you offer base options other than E26 medium?</div></div>
        <div class="faq-a">CA10 candelabra ships in E12 candelabra base. Everything else (ST, G, T, A) is E26 medium. We do not currently stock E17 intermediate, GU24 twist-lock, or G9 bi-pin in the lamp program.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="faq-item">
        <div class="faq-q"><div class="faq-num">06</div><div class="faq-text">Can I order a sample carton before specifying a project?</div></div>
        <div class="faq-a">Yes. Sample requests for hospitality and retail spec writers ship same-week from Riverside, CA. Contact your rep or sales@archipelagolighting.com with the project name and the shapes you want to evaluate.</div>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

